      "method": "Every graph is a parabola with vertex (0,0), axis the y-axis, and y(-x)=y(x). Plot x=-2,-1,0,1,2. For a the y-values are 6.92,1.73,0,1.73,6.92; join smoothly opening upward with minimum 0. For b they are -59.2,-14.8,0,-14.8,-59.2; join smoothly opening downward with maximum 0. For c and d the values are 4a,a,0,a,4a; join smoothly upward for a>0 and downward for a<0. For u<v<=0, v^2-u^2=(v-u)(v+u)<0, so positive a gives decrease and negative a gives increase. For 0<=u<v the same product is positive and the directions reverse. None is monotone on all R. Open intervals excluding 0 are also an acceptable convention for the monotone branches; the turning point must still be stated."
