    {
      "exercise": "798", "sourceNumber": "798",
      "answers": ["The expression equals 2+5/x; for every x>5, 2<2+5/x<3."],
      "method": "For x>5 the factors x, x-5, x+5 are all positive, so every denominator is nonzero and the cancellations are legal. Factor x^2-5x=x(x-5), x^2-25=(x-5)(x+5). Multiply the bracket by (x^2-25)/5: (x+5)^2/(5x)-x/5=((x+5)^2-x^2)/(5x)=(10x+25)/(5x)=2+5/x. Since x>5, 0<5/x<1; adding 2 proves BOTH strict bounds. Neither equality is attained."
